From 37986d8cf334afbf8b682265e40d1e8544cbbf3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 01:02:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] patches: add NanoPi R2S Plus Wi-Fi support to OpenWrt

FriendlyElec offers an RTL8822CS SDIO module for the M.2 slot of the
NanoPi R2S Plus. OpenWrt does not support it yet. Add the seven OpenWrt
commits that make it work as Gluon OpenWrt patches.

The first three fix the IO domain supplies of the R2S Plus, raise the
drive strength of the RK3328 sdmmc0ext pins to 8 mA and describe the
Wi-Fi module in the device tree. At 4 mA the SDIO link has round trip
times of up to 210 ms.

The next two fix an AP mode stall of rtw88. rtw88 queues every
broadcast and multicast frame for delivery after the DTIM beacon. On
SDIO these frames use up the TX pages, and the beacon download fails.
The first patch backports the fix of rtw-next for USB. The second
applies the same mapping to SDIO and PCIe.

The last two add 802.11s mesh point support to rtw88. rtw88 has one
beacon slot only, so the radio runs either a mesh or an AP interface.
Gluon's default of mesh and client AP on one radio does not work on
this module.

OpenWrt added two rtw88 patches since the Wi-Fi patches were written.
The rtw88 patches are therefore renumbered to rtl/004 to rtl/010, and
three of them are refreshed. The patches apply on the OpenWrt commit
Gluon uses. They were tested on the R2S Plus with OpenWrt main r37622
(Linux 6.18.55, backports 7.2).

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5-1 Claude:claude-fable-5-2 Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
