diff --git a/patches/openwrt/0026-mac80211-rtw88-add-802.11s-mesh-point-support.patch b/patches/openwrt/0026-mac80211-rtw88-add-802.11s-mesh-point-support.patch
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..053ab6fb
--- /dev/null
+++ b/patches/openwrt/0026-mac80211-rtw88-add-802.11s-mesh-point-support.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,412 @@
+From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
+Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 17:20:18 +0200
+Subject: mac80211: rtw88: add 802.11s mesh point support
+
+rtw88 does not offer the mesh point interface type. Upstream removed it
+in 2024 because it had never been made to work. The leftover mesh setup
+treats a mesh interface like an AP, but the driver never runs the AP
+start code for it, drops the beacons of mesh peers after a scan, keeps
+every peer at RSSI zero and would apply its own group key to the group
+frames of the peers.
+
+Advertise mesh point on the 8822C as the only interface on the radio,
+run the AP setup when the mesh beacon is enabled and undo it when the
+interface goes idle, keep the BSSID filter off while mesh is up, match
+peers by address for the RSSI and use software crypto for mesh keys.
+Mesh next to an AP or station interface is refused, since the driver
+beacons on one port only and the hardware finds group keys by their
+index alone.
+
+Tested on the NanoPi R2S Plus against an ath10k peer on channel 36 at
+80 MHz. An open mesh peers, also after scans and rejoins, and carries
+55 to 61 Mbit/s towards the board and 27 Mbit/s from it. AP and station
+mode perform as without the patch. An earlier form also ran broadcast
+floods, a 10 minute soak and batman-adv. The patch goes to
+linux-wireless.
+
+Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
+Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5-2 Claude:claude-opus-5-5
+
